//!
//! Layout rules (derived from observing the original program): the text area has a horizontal
//! margin of 5 cells; the number of lines is *estimated* as `ceil(width(prompt) / area_width)`
//! (the paragraph is word wrapped and may need a different number of lines). A single-line
//! prompt is centred and placed on row `(height - 1) / 2`; longer prompts are left aligned,
//! start on row `(height - lines - 1) / 2` and get `lines + 1` rows. With a time limit the
//! remaining seconds (bold + dim, centred) are drawn where the prompt would otherwise start,
